5
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:43,950
(Oh! My Guard)

6
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:45,080
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

7
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:47,050
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:48,850
Trust me.

9
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:50,490
I am that kiddo...

10
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:52,620
right now

11
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:58,430
- What? - And this is not comfort,

12
00:00:59,830 --> 00:01:00,830
but treatment.

13
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:30,760
Hae Ra?

14
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:39,840
See...

15
00:01:40,970 --> 00:01:42,010
I am still...

16
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:55,420
May I have your attention, please?

17
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:58,760
- The fire alarm has been activated, - Chairman.

18
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:01,330
And we are currently checking for a fire.

19
00:02:01,390 --> 00:02:02,860
- Fire. - Fire.

20
00:02:04,130 --> 00:02:05,460
- Fire. - Fire.

21
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:07,730
Please stay calm and follow the instructions...

22
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,670
to evacuate the building.

23
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,770
You can go to the right.

24
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:16,140
Please head that way. Yes. To the right.

25
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:18,610
Fire, fire.

26
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:24,780
If we get caught, the fine is at least a few hundred dollars.

27
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:27,090
Why did you make me do this?

28
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:29,520
Even so, I can't believe you let me see...

29
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:30,990
Tae Bong's limited-edition coat on a secondhand site.

30
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:33,830
You listened well, so we are even.

31
00:02:34,490 --> 00:02:35,990
Seriously, you are letting this go, right?

32
00:02:36,230 --> 00:02:38,100
- Deal. - Thanks, ma'am.

33
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,000
Tae Bong.

34
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:43,030
I really wanted to cure him...

35
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:44,240
I guess this method did not work either.

36
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:46,000
No, it's fine.

37
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:48,210
No one noticed. It is okay.

38
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:50,540
Let us move him to a room first and figure this out.

39
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:53,080
No. Let us get him to a hospital first.

40
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:56,510
How how long have you been standing there?

41
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:59,280
(Woori Hospital)

42
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:04,460
Doctor. You do not have to examine him that thoroughly.

43
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,070
This must have hurt quite a bit. Is he an idiot?

44
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,450
My pick was prettier.

45
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:31,980
The blue one.

46
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:37,020
It was more elegant.

47
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,200
But is that the reason?

48
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:48,870
I was wondering if that is really the reason.

49
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:51,800
The reason he is lying in there right now.

50
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:56,810
Does this happen every time?

51
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:04,320
It must have been hard for him. Tae Bong.

52
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:07,890
Tell him when he wakes up.

53
00:04:08,590 --> 00:04:10,120
That I am a very clueless person.

54
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:14,060
Yes. I will.

55
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:30,270
Thank you so much.

56
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,940
Gosh, that scared me.

57
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,610
What happened?

58
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,990
- As expected... - Hey, my heart almost...

59
00:04:41,090 --> 00:04:42,150
shrank in half earlier. Gosh.

60
00:04:42,250 --> 00:04:44,360
In front of so many people, that was a first.

61
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:45,790
Here. Get up. Let us go.

62
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:48,160
I will prescribe painkillers and a back brace,

63
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,730
so rest for three or four days.

64
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:52,000
Then it will heal on its own. You will be fully recovered.

65
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:01,170
He looks like a master physician, but cannot treat a patient.

66
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:03,110
You collapse like this just from locking lips,

67
00:05:03,170 --> 00:05:04,410
so should you wear a brace on your lips?

68
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:08,110
- Goodness, let us hurry up and go. - It does not make any sense...

69
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:11,580
that the actor suddenly disappeared. And with all of his staff, too.

70
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,820
Regarding the event ending so abruptly,

71
00:05:13,890 --> 00:05:16,550
we promise to compensate every single guest.

72
00:05:16,550 --> 00:05:18,560
Forget about that. Either call...

73
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:22,660
the actor again, or tell me where Tae Bong is.

74
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:24,700
As the event organiser,

75
00:05:24,930 --> 00:05:28,500
we have no obligation to answer someone who is not even a VVIP.

76
00:05:28,570 --> 00:05:30,540
I offer my deepest apologies.

77
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,570
Are you ignoring me right now because I am not a VVIP...

78
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:34,310
Then you can tell me this, right?

79
00:05:34,370 --> 00:05:35,810
That man who was standing next to the podium.

80
00:05:36,410 --> 00:05:39,940
You know, the one who gave off that dandy and modern vibe.

81
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:43,050
Does he happen to work here? Did he come from London?

82
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:44,580
What is his name?

83
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,920
Hey...

84
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,420
I am telling you, it is definitely him.

85
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:48,750
He is the exact same man I saw...

86
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:49,920
when I went to London after my project.

87
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:51,120
He was so impressive...

88
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:52,290
that I modelled the male lead character...

89
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,960
in The Crown Prince's Bodyguard exactly after him.

90
00:05:54,030 --> 00:05:56,030
- I understand. - Excuse me. I am right, am I not?

91
00:05:56,090 --> 00:05:59,430
- What is his name? Han Jung Woo... - Stop it.

92
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:01,430
Stop it and let us go. I am so tired.

93
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:05,300
- All right. - I will pack my bags and come down.

94
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:07,110
We should head up to Seoul, even if it is late.

95
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:17,010
It is not like he actually cannot kiss...

96
00:06:17,650 --> 00:06:19,620
Then does that mean he has been lying...

97
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:21,320
and scamming the entire nation?

98
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:24,490
Was that real?

99
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,530
Of all times, at that exact moment...

100
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,700
How do I verify this?

101
00:06:36,870 --> 00:06:38,600
We meet here again, Reporter Yeo.

102
00:06:38,670 --> 00:06:41,970
- It is nice to see you. - It is nice to see you, too.

103
00:06:42,170 --> 00:06:44,180
Were you invited as a VVIP, too, Na Ri?

104
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:46,980
I am here as Tae Bong's girlfriend.

105
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,950
I paid my own money and came on my own.

106
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:51,250
Right, then I will see you later.

107
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:53,580
Reporter Yeo, what is wrong with your skin?

108
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:55,290
Have you been having a really hard time lately?

109
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:58,860
- What is wrong with my skin? - It is all red and breaking out,

110
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:00,460
and your tone is completely ruined.

111
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:02,960
What should we do? I am so upset for you.

112
00:07:03,030 --> 00:07:04,430
I have something good for that.

113
00:07:10,370 --> 00:07:11,500
Hey, Song Na Ri, you,

114
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:14,110
- what are you doing right now? - Tae Bong told me this.

115
00:07:14,170 --> 00:07:15,240
Whether a talk or your skin,

116
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:16,440
this is what you do when it is dry.

117
00:07:16,510 --> 00:07:17,940
Ever since the party earlier,

118
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:20,110
your skin looked like a dried squid.

119
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:22,750
No need to thank me. I will be going.

120
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:25,120
So moisturizing.

121
00:07:29,250 --> 00:07:30,920
Did she just insult me?

122
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,190
Does she know something, too?

123
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,360
Well, look at her.

124
00:07:38,030 --> 00:07:39,200
Just taking care of her man.

125
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:41,930
Careful.

126
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:46,840
I will raise the bed for you.

127
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:52,510
Hey, why are you actually getting hospitalised?

128
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:53,610
It is not like this is the first time.

129
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,080
No, seriously, the timing makes it look like...

130
00:07:55,150 --> 00:07:56,450
he passed out from the kiss.

131
00:07:57,110 --> 00:07:58,120
You little...

132
00:07:58,980 --> 00:08:01,190
Everyone there probably thought the same thing.

133
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,790
The reason he completely passed out.

134
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:08,490
Hey, Tae Bong. Just like he said, the timing is a bit questionable.

135
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,430
Someone might have seen you in all that chaos,

136
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,030
and the BK Director is outside right now...

137
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,100
- If we raise suspicion... - No. Since this afternoon,

138
00:08:14,170 --> 00:08:16,100
he has been sweating profusely.

139
00:08:16,270 --> 00:08:19,040
His schedule was too packed, and he really needs to rest.

140
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:21,610
He is still sweating a lot right now.

141
00:08:23,510 --> 00:08:26,510
Hey. All right, fine. Then let us just say it was because...

142
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:28,650
of his packed schedule. Let us get our stories straight.

143
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:35,420
Are you feeling any better?

144
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:38,360
Well, as you can see.

145
00:08:38,890 --> 00:08:42,490
Even in this dull hospital gown, my face still shines.

146
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:46,230
This is all my fault. You know, overwork.

147
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:47,370
I got too greedy with his schedule, so...

148
00:08:47,470 --> 00:08:50,130
Yes. I hope you recover quickly.

149
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:01,950
Hey.

150
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:05,980
You were all dressed up in a gown earlier.

151
00:09:06,050 --> 00:09:10,420
Why did you climb up on the stage? And you kissed him?

152
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:13,490
- A kiss? - Su Dong.

153
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:21,300
Think of the person on the receiving end. Because of your lips,

154
00:09:21,370 --> 00:09:25,300
his legs gave out. He was just so dumbfounded.

155
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:28,010
No matter how much you throw yourself at him,

156
00:09:28,070 --> 00:09:30,070
he will not even bat an eye.

157
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:31,540
Do you know what kind of person he is?

158
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:33,340
The female celebrities he has dated could line up in four rows...

159
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:35,750
and circle the parade ground two times.

160
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:37,620
- Yang Soo Dong. - I will handle this.

161
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:39,320
And where did you get the money?

162
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,750
Do you even have money?

163
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:43,720
Do you think that charity gala earlier was child's play?

164
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:47,360
If you look closely, she is going to cause a really big incident.

165
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:50,060
I can see it in her face. Right, CEO Park?

166
00:09:54,830 --> 00:09:57,070
Put your hands down. Put them down. Attention.

167
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,470
Your face is going to cause a bigger incident.

168
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:02,710
I should just sew your mouth shut right now.

169
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:03,870
Seriously.

170
00:10:05,110 --> 00:10:06,140
I apologize.

171
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:08,650
- I am sorry. - Why are you...

172
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:11,450
You even changed your clothes?

173
00:10:11,450 --> 00:10:13,880
We are going to leave now and leave him with Su Dong.

174
00:10:13,950 --> 00:10:14,950
No.

175
00:10:15,690 --> 00:10:16,720
Why?

176
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:20,220
Are you uncomfortable with Su Dong? You are both men.

177
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:23,890
The doctor said I need absolute rest earlier.

178
00:10:24,230 --> 00:10:26,630
For rest, it is best to have someone with zero presence,

179
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:28,200
but Su Dong's presence is way too big.

180
00:10:28,630 --> 00:10:30,230
Sometimes I even feel overshadowed by him.

181
00:10:30,530 --> 00:10:31,770
- Me? - Him?

182
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,140
- Since when? - Since when?

183
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:35,240
I will stay.

184
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:38,540
If he needs absolute rest,

185
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:41,580
- it makes sense for me to stay. - I mean, why you?

186
00:10:42,110 --> 00:10:44,580
Well, that is...

187
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:47,890
I have the least presence here.

188
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:51,190
Plus, rest is a matter of safety.

189
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:56,130
Are you just using that as an excuse to aggressively hit on him again?

190
00:10:56,390 --> 00:10:59,200
Tae Bong, she is seriously hitting on you.

191
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,200
Just shut up.

192
00:11:00,560 --> 00:11:01,670
Shut up.

193
00:11:01,730 --> 00:11:03,500
Hey, do not do that. Why are you hitting him?

194
00:11:03,570 --> 00:11:05,570
Stand at attention, stand at attention. Not there, here.

195
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:07,810
That is right. Right there.

196
00:11:08,170 --> 00:11:10,440
Right here. Use your knee, hit him right in the groin with your knee.

197
00:11:10,510 --> 00:11:11,880
That is right. One more time, one more time.

198
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:12,980
Harder, do it properly.

199
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,350
No, that was not clean. Not clean.

200
00:11:14,410 --> 00:11:15,450
One, two, three.

201
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:19,080
(Woori Hospital)

202
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:35,630
(Woori Hospital)

203
00:11:42,610 --> 00:11:44,610
Hong Du, will it not be too hard for you?

204
00:11:45,710 --> 00:11:47,040
I am perfectly fine.

205
00:11:47,210 --> 00:11:49,080
My body is built from doing part-time jobs.

206
00:11:49,150 --> 00:11:50,880
Even on a concrete floor, as long as I lie down,

207
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,020
I can fall right asleep.

208
00:11:52,350 --> 00:11:54,990
Part-time jobs? You must have done a lot. Oh, right.

209
00:11:55,190 --> 00:11:57,120
Oh, right. The sicker a person is,

210
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:59,120
the closer you need to stick to them.

211
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,620
Right. Very close. Right?

212
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,990
If she sticks close to him, she will just hit on him again.

213
00:12:11,770 --> 00:12:15,510
- Are you really okay by yourself? - I am really okay.

214
00:12:15,770 --> 00:12:17,040
You do not need to worry.

215
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:19,040
I should stay here with you,

216
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:21,810
but work is crazy right now because I am not there.

217
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:27,490
I feel a bit bad leaving you all alone, Hong Du.

218
00:12:27,550 --> 00:12:29,350
You do not need to feel bad at all,

219
00:12:29,890 --> 00:12:30,890
so hurry up and go, Mr. Han.

220
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:33,690
I am sorry.

221
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:35,490
Get back safely.

222
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:05,190
By any chance...

223
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:07,860
Did it steal your money?

224
00:13:15,930 --> 00:13:16,970
Hold on a second.

225
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:24,310
I think it ate your money.

226
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:41,090
Do you happen to have...

227
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:43,160
another one-dollar bill?

228
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:51,400
I do not carry any cash on me.

229
00:13:54,970 --> 00:13:56,470
Will this work?

230
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:04,380
What do you want to drink?

231
00:14:10,690 --> 00:14:11,760
There we go.

232
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:15,460
Darn it.

233
00:14:15,530 --> 00:14:17,490
It should respect its elders, but it just steals their money.

234
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,070
Anyway, machines these days have absolutely no manners.

235
00:14:33,410 --> 00:14:34,410
Well then.

236
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:36,710
Excuse me.

237
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:40,320
Well...

238
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:43,490
Could you keep me company for a little while?

239
00:14:48,830 --> 00:14:49,830
Pardon?

240
00:14:51,830 --> 00:14:53,730
You and your daughter went that long...

241
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,430
without really speaking to each other?

242
00:14:57,270 --> 00:14:59,370
I would not be able to last a single day.

243
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,440
Then again,

244
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:05,180
I can never be separated from my father now, either.

245
00:15:10,650 --> 00:15:11,650
Your father...

246
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:15,620
You two must have a good relationship?

247
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,620
Actually,

248
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,230
until recently, I thought my dad and I...

249
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:24,090
were separated forever.

250
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:26,430
But...

251
00:15:27,830 --> 00:15:29,970
we met again like a miracle,

252
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:33,070
and he doesn't really recognise me.

253
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:37,110
And I'm only just now starting to truly see him.

254
00:15:42,810 --> 00:15:45,920
I'm sure you're a good father, just like my dad.

255
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:47,950
Because you're worrying about your daughter this much.

256
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:50,990
Seeing how you're expressing your concern...

257
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,990
to a complete stranger like me.

258
00:15:55,530 --> 00:15:56,860
Chairman, have you returned?

259
00:16:00,430 --> 00:16:01,970
The young lady isn't asleep yet.

260
00:16:13,110 --> 00:16:14,210
I'll see her later.

261
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,970
If I reach out first, even now,

262
00:16:39,470 --> 00:16:41,140
do you think we could change?

263
00:16:47,410 --> 00:16:48,410
She's probably...

264
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:51,220
waiting eagerly for you.

265
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:57,090
So stop getting ripped off by that rude vending machine,

266
00:16:57,150 --> 00:16:58,360
and hurry home.

267
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:03,190
Good fathers like you are supposed to go home early.

268
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:07,500
Tae Bong is probably looking for me.

269
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:09,500
Well then.

270
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,370
(Woori Hospital)

271
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,470
Get home safely.

272
00:17:12,970 --> 00:17:13,970
Do you think...

273
00:17:17,910 --> 00:17:19,210
We'll see each other again?

274
00:17:21,610 --> 00:17:22,650
Of course.

275
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:26,450
You borrowed a whole dollar from me.

276
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:29,050
And I'm a very petty creditor.

277
00:17:34,530 --> 00:17:37,860
- Where are you? Aren't you coming? - I know, I'm coming.

278
00:18:19,470 --> 00:18:20,470
Song Na Ri.

279
00:18:22,070 --> 00:18:23,070
Is something wrong?

280
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:27,010
- No, I'm just craving a beer. - Aren't you hungry?

281
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,780
If you haven't eaten, do you want to eat together?

282
00:18:28,850 --> 00:18:30,110
I'm not in the mood to eat.

283
00:18:31,010 --> 00:18:33,220
But this is a bit much for one person to eat.

284
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:35,350
Do you really think I'll eat with you?

285
00:18:35,450 --> 00:18:36,650
I'm on a diet.

286
00:18:37,490 --> 00:18:39,720
- What is it? - Take care of yourself.

287
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:40,920
I asked what that is.

288
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:46,460
What are you doing?

289
00:18:46,530 --> 00:18:48,470
Aren't you going to put the noodles and powder in?

290
00:18:48,830 --> 00:18:49,900
Song Na Ri.

291
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:52,440
Why do you think there's a recipe on this ramyeon package?

292
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:53,870
It's telling us that...

293
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:57,040
cooking it this way makes it taste the best.

294
00:18:57,510 --> 00:19:00,740
We really don't click. Move aside.

295
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,250
Are you in a cooking competition or something?

296
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:07,180
Where did you even get latex gloves? Seriously.

297
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,690
You're just eating ramyeon...

298
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:10,190
That's hot, darn it.

299
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:15,760
You spilled the powder everywhere. You can't cook, can you?

300
00:19:15,990 --> 00:19:17,790
That's because we deviated from the recipe.

301
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:21,230
That looks delicious. The noodles...

302
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:23,600
If you lift the noodles like this,

303
00:19:23,670 --> 00:19:26,100
- that's not going to work. - Be quiet.

304
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:27,500
Do you not want to eat?

305
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:44,320
It's better than my recipe.

306
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:49,530
- I have one question, though. - Sure.

307
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:51,360
When you watch Korean dramas,

308
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,500
when a woman is hitting on a guy, she always...

309
00:19:53,630 --> 00:19:55,530
asks, "Do you want to come over for ramyeon?"

310
00:19:56,470 --> 00:19:57,530
Why is it ramyeon?

311
00:19:57,870 --> 00:19:59,100
Do you really not know?

312
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,870
The profound philosophy behind ramyeon?

313
00:20:02,510 --> 00:20:03,510
Philosophy?

314
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:07,240
I guess this dating expert has to teach you.

315
00:20:09,010 --> 00:20:11,210
Koreans naturally unite over food...

316
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:16,650
Wait, I mean, come together? Anyway, out of all foods, ramyeon...

317
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,490
is a lot like a something between a man and a woman.

318
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:20,660
A something?

319
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:22,830
What do you think is the most important part of a something?

320
00:20:22,890 --> 00:20:24,960
It is the signal that tells you the timing.

321
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,530
Now, the water just started boiling.

322
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:30,100
Then you signal the noodles and soup to go in.

323
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,440
But if you rush it at that timing?

324
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:32,540
Then it will not work.

325
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,040
Put in the noodles and soup, and wait three minutes.

326
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,210
This is the art of waiting.

327
00:20:35,270 --> 00:20:36,940
But also, the contact between the air and the noodles...

328
00:20:37,010 --> 00:20:38,640
determines how chewy the noodles get.

329
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:43,210
And this is exactly like a kiss. Half inhaling, half exhaling.

330
00:20:44,450 --> 00:20:45,880
And this is the most important part.

331
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:48,690
Actually, with ramyeon, any recipe does not matter at all.

332
00:20:48,790 --> 00:20:50,850
Ramyeon is always delicious when you eat it at night.

333
00:20:51,590 --> 00:20:52,660
And what comes next?

334
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,160
A steamy night.

335
00:20:57,360 --> 00:20:58,360
A steamy night?

336
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,330
If you had something and even kissed,

337
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,730
you definitely have to make it a steamy night.

338
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,770
Eating ramyeon together on a steamy night means...

339
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:06,840
game over.

340
00:21:07,670 --> 00:21:10,670
Well, I will leave the rest to your imagination.

341
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,410
So earlier, like this...

342
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:16,510
Well, if you understand, hurry up and eat. The ramyeon will get soggy.

343
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:21,620
How do you know all of this?

344
00:21:22,290 --> 00:21:24,050
Come to think of it, out of everyone I know,

345
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:25,360
Na Ri, you are the smartest.

346
00:21:28,560 --> 00:21:30,130
